Description: Announce the desktop file name as the Wayland app id
 A Wayland compositor finds a window's icon by looking for a desktop file named
 after the app id the window advertises. GTK derives that from the program
 name, which defaults to the executable, so the window announced
 slic3r-app-launcher while the installed desktop file is
 com.prusa3d.PrusaSlicer, and no icon was found. StartupWMClass cannot fix it:
 that describes WM_CLASS, which only exists on X11, and KWin matches Wayland
 windows on the app id alone.
Author: Jason Scurtu <github@mail.scurtu.me>
